    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0622" n="494" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg494"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 351.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to
                        Mr. Langston</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 13,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 331.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I herewith transmit for your information a
                    copy of a communication<anchor n="*" xml:id="d351-f1"/> from Mr. E. D. Bassett,
                    of the 13th ultimo, in regard to the case of Mr. C. A. Van Bokkelen; also one
                    from Mr. C. A. Van Bokkelen himself, of the 18th of December last, in the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I have stated to Mr. Bassett that although I bad given his letter attentive
                    perusal, I was disinclined to transfer to Washington a discussion of the merits
                    of Mr. Van Bokkelen’s case, and that your action in his behalf to secure for him
                    impartial treatment had received the Department’s approval.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d351-a1.xml" xpointer="d351-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
